  "body": "The maintainer asked for this change on 2026-11-23: \"Do your changes as a docs changes, push it and merge it and announce it one go.. On my call.\"\n\nWhat the data shows (30 PRs, 2026-11-20 to 2026-11-23, 36 times a ready PR went back to draft):\n- 27 of 36 followed a `needs-rework` label. 17 came from our own reviews and 10 from the author's reviewer.\n- 3 followed a `conflicts` label. 6 had no label cause.\n- The median time from ready to draft is 1.6 hours.\n- #3283 and #3284 flipped three times each. #3061 returned four times for one class of defect.\n\nEach round trip costs one more read and one more trial.\n\nThe change:\n1. A `needs-rework` finding does not turn a ready PR back into a draft. The author pushes the fix to the same PR. A push moves the head, so the earlier review and `merge-ready` do not count for the new head.\n2. An orange `conflicts` verdict still makes one of our own PRs a draft.\n3. The first `needs-rework` comment names the class of each finding and asks for one rule that closes the class.\n\nDone means: AGENTS.md, the `review-prs` skill and the `resolve-conflicts` skill say this, a decision file records the maintainer's order, and PROCESS_VERSION is bumped and announced on #681.\n",
